WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.200
Speaker 1: We're continuing to follow the
impact of different vaccine requirements,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.540
and some of the most interesting ones to look
at are actually the ones for the military.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:15.269
We learned from Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin
that the military would be indeed implementing

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:17.279
an actual vaccine mandate.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:19.650
Speaker 2: It's just you've just got to
Speaker 1: get vaccinated, that it is not

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.900
a protocol where you can test out, you got
to be vaccinated.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.039
And we are now starting to see the first discharges
from the military for vaccine refusal.

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:32.419
Now the right is making a big deal out of
this and framing it as unpatriotic.

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:34.840
Joe Biden,
Speaker 2: by making service

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.620
Speaker 1: members get vaccinated and losing
service

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.059
Speaker 2: members refusing to get
Speaker 1: vaccinated is weakening the military

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:47.050
and is therefore unpatriotic and a socialist
and a Marxist and a communist and right like

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.040
follow it along to the whole thing.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.579
Twenty seven people have been discharged.

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:53.100
Speaker 2: Ladies and gentlemen, that is that
is that what

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.379
Speaker 1: we know so far.

00:00:54.379 --> 00:01:00.699
The Air Force has discharged 27 service members
were refusing the COVID vaccine.

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:05.620
These are the first service members to be
involuntarily discharged for refusing the

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.760
vaccine.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:12.430
Spokesperson for the Air Force said they received
counseling about the vaccines.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.850
They still refused and commanders made the
decision to discharge

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:18.560
Speaker 2: them for refusing
Speaker 1: to comply

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:24.490
Speaker 2: with that requirement,
Speaker 1: considered to be a lawful order.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:29.260
All 27 of these individuals were with the
Air Force under six years.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:34.350
There may have been additional reasons for
the discharge, but the COVID vaccine refusal

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.040
was
Speaker 2: at least one of those reasons.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.690
Speaker 1: Now they announced this back in
August, so they had August, September, October,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.690
November.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.470
We are now in December.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:50.530
The Air Force had a deadline of November 2nd,
which was one of the earlier deadlines.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.040
And of course, you don't immediately remove
the people on November 2nd.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:57.180
You've got to go through a process and that
has now taken place.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:03.750
Each branch of the military has its own process
for discharge, and they all include We're

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.170
going to counsel you about the vaccine.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.039
We're going to educate you about the vaccine.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:10.869
Then there will be disciplinary action.

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:15.180
You will still have an opportunity to get
vaccinated, and only after that will we start

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.280
with the discharges.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:22.380
And what is fascinating about it is that what
the right says is a horribly authoritarian

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:27.450
thing is no one something that has been in
the military for, what, a hundred years.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.200
Speaker 2: I mean, I don't even know
Speaker 1: when the first military vaccine

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:36.740
requirement came in, but in particular in
the military, there have been so many vaccine

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:40.150
requirements that nobody questioned for so
long.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:45.980
So no one, if this is authoritarian, where
have you been all this time?

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.390
Speaker 2: That's the
Speaker 1: first issue.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:50.870
Speaker 2: The second is that even the way
Speaker 1: they're handling

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.430
Speaker 2: this is eminently
Speaker 1: reasonable.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:03:01.430
I'm reminded of the segment we recently did
where Tucker Carlson criticized a CNN host

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:05.100
named Brian Stelter because Brian Stelter
fired his nanny.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.610
He fired his nanny because she wouldn't get
vaccinated to be around his kid.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:12.080
And when you listen to Brian Stelter, explain
it, he says, Yeah, you know, we really like

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.560
the nanny.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.710
And so
Speaker 2: we said, Let's wait

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:16.710
Speaker 1: six months.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.420
She doesn't want the vaccine, but let's wait
six months because she'll see that it's safe

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.000
and she'll come to the decision on her own
that she's going to get the vaccine to protect

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.000
our kid or kids.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.670
I don't remember how many, and she still didn't
do it.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.680
So it was really tough.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.650
But we did let her go because we want someone
vaccinated around our kid.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:33.900
Eminently reasonable.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:39.251
And here with the military, it's we're giving
you months notice that by November 2nd, you've

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.960
got to be vaccinated.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.960
You refuse.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.530
We're going to give you counseling.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.160
If you refuse, we're going to give you education.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.380
Speaker 2: We will then just give you write
it

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.190
Speaker 1: up and still not discharge you.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:54.230
Speaker 2: It is endlessly, endlessly
Speaker 1: reasonable for a group that historically

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.200
just line up and get vaccinated.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.440
Speaker 2: That's it.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.050
Now the
Speaker 1: other takeaway here

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.500
Speaker 2: is that the vaccine
Speaker 1: requirements really work.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:07.310
Speaker 2: The Pentagon shows
Speaker 1: that about 90 percent of the active

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:14.570
duty forces vaccinated and 74 percent of the
total force, including reserves and the National

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:18.620
Guard, that's significantly more than the
general population.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.239
Of course, it's made up of
Speaker 2: adults, so we've got to make sure

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.580
we're
Speaker 1: comparing apples to apples, so

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.840
we're going to continue to see what
Speaker 2: happens elsewhere.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.150
So far, just 27 people.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.130
Speaker 1: And so anybody telling you this
is unpatriotic and weakening the military,

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.260
it's
Speaker 2: 27

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:38.440
Speaker 1: people from the Air Force Army
deadline is December 15th.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.000
There will be another deadline like the final
final final deadline is the Army National

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.000
Guard.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.880
That's not until June of 2022.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.520
So those are the latest numbers as we now
understand them.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.540
Remember, we were told we may lose tens of
thousands of service members here.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.560
So far, it's 27.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.560
We were told we might.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.340
Lose a third of NYPD.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.800
It was what some type was it, 34 people or
something along those lines.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.180
United Airlines, there's going to be no flights.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.810
There's going to be no nothing.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.480
Almost everybody is vaccinated
Speaker 2: now at United

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.280
Speaker 1: Airlines, so it's really a twofer
at the end of the day in the sense that you

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.050
improve the overall health of your personnel,
you reduce the risk that your personnel are

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:28.060
going to contract COVID and be sick and be
out, et cetera.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.750
But we're also getting rid of some of the
wackiest people.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.730
As we've said before, there's probably if
you imagine a van diagram

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.180
Speaker 2: of police
Speaker 1: we don't want because of reasons

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:43.699
other than they don't want the vaccine, either
use of force, not the types of people we want

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:45.840
and police that don't want the vaccine.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.780
There's probably a lot of overlap there.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.800
We're probably getting rid of a bunch of those
